2.43.0

From: Pankaj Gupta <pankaj.gupta@nxp.com>

Adds the driver for communication interface to secure-enclave, that
enables exchanging messages with NXP secure enclave HW IP(s)
like EdgeLock Enclave, from:
- User-Space Applications via character driver.

ABI documentation for the NXP secure-enclave driver.

User-space library using this driver:
- i.MX Secure Enclave library:
  -- URL: https://github.com/nxp-imx/imx-secure-enclave.git,
- i.MX Secure Middle-Ware:
  -- URL: https://github.com/nxp-imx/imx-smw.git

Following checks are performed on the incoming msg-header,
to block exchanging invalid arbitrary commands:
- maximum allowed words,
- check if command-tag & response-tag are valid
- version,
- command id validation check, to allow limited base-line API(s)
  and restrict following:
  - exchanging power management commands.
  - reset requests.
  - BBSM configuration requests.
  - re-initializing the FW.
  - RNG init
  - CAAM resource release management
  - SE's internal memory management.
from user-space.

Signed-off-by: Pankaj Gupta <pankaj.gupta@nxp.com>
---
Changes from v46 to v47:

1. schedule_work() UAF fix: moved inside clbk_rx_lock; cancel_work_sync()
   added before kfree(priv) in se_if_priv_release().

2. goto/scoped_guard fix: bool list_was_empty + break replaces goto.

3. TOCTOU comment: advisory early check noted; FW rejects second
   ELE_STORAGE_OPEN_REQ itself.

4. se_val_rsp_hdr_n_status: add act_rx_msg_sz output to ele_msg_send_rcv()
   to capture actual received bytes under clbk_rx_lock. Move size check
   after status check; return -ENOSPC on size mismatch.
   All callers updated.

5. fw_api_specific_ops(): void→int return type, single se_close_storage() call, interrupted path returns 0.
   Error propagated on success path, ioctl aborts cleanly on registration failure.
   Updating the declaration in ele_fw_api.h to match.

6. single modify_lock acquisition capturing receiver_exists + is_cmd_receiver atomically, eliminating redundant scoped_guard in ELE_STORAGE_OPEN_REQ
